unit BCrypt;

{ Translated from bcrypt.h (Windows SDK 10.0.26100), with the NTSTATUS
  values of ntstatus.h that the BCrypt functions return: algorithm
  providers, properties, hashing and HMAC, symmetric and authenticated
  encryption, asymmetric keys, signatures, secret agreement, key derivation
  and random numbers.

  bcrypt.dll does not exist before Windows Vista, so every function is bound
  at run time on first use, and programs that use this unit still start on
  Windows XP. bcrypt.dll is loaded once, by full path from the system
  directory (no search-order planting), and stays loaded; each function
  pointer is cached once found. When the DLL or an export is missing (any
  function on Windows XP; BCryptDeriveKeyCapi and BCryptDeriveKeyPBKDF2
  before Windows 7, BCryptKeyDerivation before Windows 8,
  BCryptCreateMultiHash and BCryptProcessMultiOperations before Windows 8.1,
  BCryptHash before Windows 10):
    - the NTSTATUS functions return STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED ($C0000002) and
      set their handle and count out parameters to nil / 0;
    - BCryptFreeBuffer does nothing.
  The helpers at the end of the interface (not in the SDK) fail the same
  way: they return STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED or an empty string.

  NTSTATUS is a Longint; failures are negative (BCRYPT_SUCCESS). The STATUS_*
  constants are typed NTSTATUS so that they compare correctly with the
  results. Windows.pas declares STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE and STATUS_NO_MEMORY
  as DWORD exception codes; where BCrypt follows Windows in a uses clause,
  the NTSTATUS constants of this unit hide them (Windows.STATUS_NO_MEMORY
  still names the DWORD constant, for exception records).

  The string identifiers (algorithms, properties, blob types, chaining
  modes, KDFs) are typed PWideChar constants with the text of the SDK's
  L"..." macros. Pass them to the PWideChar parameters directly; to set a
  string property use BCryptSetStringProperty, which passes the terminating
  null character too.

  Records use the default alignment ($A8), like the SDK: the ULONGLONG
  cbData of BCRYPT_AUTHENTICATED_CIPHER_MODE_INFO is at offset 48, and the
  record is 64 bytes on x86.

  Not declared here: the CryptoConfig functions and structures
  (BCryptQueryProviderRegistration, BCrypt*Context*, BCryptResolveProviders,
  BCryptRegisterConfigChangeNotify ...), the provider interface versions,
  and the post-quantum and XOF additions of Windows 11 24H2 (ML-DSA, ML-KEM,
  SLH-DSA, LMS, XMSS, BCryptEncapsulate/BCryptDecapsulate, parameter sets,
  cSHAKE, KMAC, BCRYPT_PKCS11_RSA_AES_WRAP_BLOB). }

{$WEAKPACKAGEUNIT ON}
{$MINENUMSIZE 4}

